headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Directwerk API collection. Mirrors ../http/*.http (JetBrains HTTP Client harness) -- 
  generated from the actual controller source, cross-checked against the harness.

  Setup:
  1. Start the API: docker compose up -d && ./gradlew :directwerk-app:bootRun (from Directwerk/)
  2. Select the "local" environment in Bruno.
  3. Open the environment and fill in the secret vars (client secrets, dev seed passwords) from your .env.
     Secrets are declared (vars:secret) but never written to these committed .bru files.
  4. Run 01-Auth-and-Tokens requests top to bottom to populate access tokens as runtime variables.
  5. Other folders use auth: inherit and pick up the token their folder.bru declares:
     platformAccessToken (Platform Admin), tenantAAccessToken (Tenant Admin/Media/Podcast Content),
     subscriberAccessToken (Me/private RSS). Re-run the matching login under 01 if a token expires
     (access token TTL 15 min) or use the refresh requests.
  6. Folders are numbered in the same dependency order as the http/ harness they were generated from.
}
